{"tool_name":"seatac","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"seatac","home":"https://github.com/gongx030/seatac","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"Tool for exploring the chromatin landscape and the role of pioneer factors.","addition_date":"2024-01-02T17:14:59.449747Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T14:24:12.865445Z","tool_type":["Library"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:seatac","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"gongx030@umn.edu","name":"Wuming Gong","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3147-4028","typeEntity":"Person"},{"email":"garry@umn.edu","name":"Daniel J. Garry","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"public"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Dot plot plotting","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0490"},{"term":"Nucleosome position prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0432"},{"term":"Peak calling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3222"}]}],"name":"SeATAC","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Pub2Tools","publication":[{"doi":"10.1186/s13059-023-02954-5","metadata":{"abstract":"Assay for Transposase-Accessible Chromatin with sequencing (ATAC-seq) reveals chromatin accessibility across the genome. Currently, no method specifically detects differential chromatin accessibility. Here, SeATAC uses a conditional variational autoencoder model to learn the latent representation of ATAC-seq V-plots and outperforms MACS2 and NucleoATAC on six separate tasks. Applying SeATAC to several pioneer factor-induced differentiation or reprogramming ATAC-seq datasets suggests that induction of these factors not only relaxes the closed chromatin but also decreases chromatin accessibility of 20% to 30% of their target sites. SeATAC is a novel tool to accurately reveal genomic regions with differential chromatin accessibility from ATAC-seq data.","authors":[{"name":"Dsouza N."},{"name":"Garry D.J."},{"name":"Gong W."}],"citationCount":1,"date":"2023-